    },
    "body": "The retained compensation artifact gained two correct entries but stalled at their next token. This change learns only the existing 960 shared-action continuation coefficients from the mechanically rebuilt current frontier, with 86 full-pool guards preserving every original success and both gained entries.\n\nOne fresh gradient orders a once-only adjacent legal-Q4 construction. U affects Generate and every physical Copy occurrence before the common clip and alias reduction. Source, Context, Potential, Generate factors/bias/prototypes, bridge, cue/prefix, tokenizer and geometry stay frozen. Transactional guards and an independently reloaded U export preserve the exact native numerical boundary.\n\nThe single executed CUDA experiment at `8eed8478e800bbd01f499bc2d9ffb9c32cd59efc` accepted 959 coordinates and rejected one. Fresh revised objective CE fell from 8.2326417554 to 4.5430571640, correcting 264 of 504 current frontiers. Actual autoregressive entry accuracy rose from 10 to 273 of 512. Complete replies remained **8/512**, with zero gained or lost complete cases, so `useful_candidate=false`. This is a retained optimization result; the original accepted Source48/Generate64 remains accepted. No useful conversation, transfer, source-role fix or energy claim is made.\n\nThe result is sealed as report `2a9f967a955c6dc40b422c94f1b6d1d54f2511a24fb601af97218d49440b9923`, manifest `6cbfabf807427f3baa2bfcfda7187e1b00f3a205ec9466b30a7437a410baad94`, 1178 files. Private HF store result revision `4b443fd8bc19860e409cb31429bab3e623dc6cf0` and runtime revision `3d226bdbc9ea4acc07f501629de5b8be4ee5015f` were freshly downloaded and hash verified.\n\nValidation at the executed source: 54 focused fitter tests, the CPU shared-Copy clip/adjoint test, and the explicitly invoked CUDA shared-Copy/native-anchor/duplicate-adjoint parity test passed, as did formatting and optimized compilation. Mathematical and adversarial source review passed. A separate saved-evidence reader independently recomputed 1764 integer objective pools, all 86 guard pools at three export endpoints, exact current-frontier/weight identities, frozen artifact identity and 1024 parent/final actual trajectories. Three Rust seal verifications passed. This audit does not recompute backward, inference or the upstream Context/cue/prefix kernels. Exact final-head checks and review are posted separately before protected merge.\n\nA saved-output census derived after result preservation records 239 remaining entry failures, 242 position-one failures, 18 position-two failures and five genuinely reached factual-token failures. The census is tracked in this delivery and separately retained with the delivery receipt; it was not in the earlier result archive. These new factual failures justify a subsequent full-pool attribution question about Source/bridge and continuation/Copy coupling. That successor is not admitted before this PR is merged; no refill, dose or unchanged experiment is proposed.\n\nThe prospective work card is issue #820 comment 6059560163. Cumulative projected allowance is 476070 seconds, preserving prior charges. Execution used two CPU threads, one owned GPU, a remote per-lab Cargo target and remote durable output. The single model supervisor took 541.249 seconds, with 1671768 KiB peak RSS; the independent saved reader took 257.453 seconds. Preparation, checks, retries, preservation and delivery remain charged in the cumulative resource ledger.\n\nReferences #820.\n",
